ukrainian troops are trying to hold off  russian attacks in much of ukraine's  east the kremlin wants to capture the  whole of the industrial donbass region  but gains are smaller and coming slower  than expected  further south on the sea of azov a  handful of civilians has been allowed to  leave a steelworks in the besieged city  of mariopol  families of those still trapped in the  port town gathered in the capital kiev  so they would not be forgotten  the anguish is etched on their faces  these women fled mariupol but their  loved ones did not  now in ukraine's capital kyiv they are  pleading for the lives of their besieged  family members  one woman says she can't eat knowing  that her husband is starving  another issued this call to action  we as wives of the defenders express our  willingness to become human shields to  make a corridor to marry yupo to protect  an international delegation  we asked the un  we ask believers of all faiths we asked  the red cross and all of them to join  our march to marry you paul  we will become a human shield for the  delegation to help evacuate our husbands  they are here in the azov style steel  plant the final holdout in ukraine's  port city of marieupol  conditions are thought to be dire  slow the deputy commander of the azov  regiment ukraine's far-right nationalist  unit reported that 20 civilians were  safely evacuated russia says 25 people  were freed from the steel plant  ukraine's president has vowed to fight  for those still trapped inside  all the leaders of the free world know  what russia has done to mariupol  russia will be held to account for this  many world leaders are trying to help  save our heroic defenders of the city  this was discussed in great detail with  the u.n secretary general during his  visit to cuve  we're doing everything everything to  ensure that the evacuation mission for  mariupol is carried out  far from mariupol in ukraine's north  authorities say they've uncovered more  evidence of alleged russian atrocities  in bucha a town now synonymous with  claims of war crimes the bodies of three  more civilians were found  police say the men had been tortured and  bound and shot in the head  with many residents in butcher still  unaccounted for survivors in the scar  town know that more grim discoveries  could still be unearthed  and for more let's bring in dw  correspondent matthias billinger who is  now in ukraine's main port city of  odessa in the southeast mathias  ukraine's military says a russian  missile hit the runway in the airport of  odessa where you're at what else do you  know  yeah yesterday shortly after we arrived  we heard three loud explosions and uh  the runway has been hit by missiles it's  destroyed it cannot be used anymore no  people have suffered in these attacks uh  and uh the missiles that hit this runway  were fired from crimea um which is the  the territory that russia has annexed in  2014.  and you were just in the capital kiev  before coming to odessa what's the  situation like there  uh the kiev is is  now for for more than a month or for  about one month  no russian troops are near kiev anymore  so life uh is a little bit is returning  to the city the city is a little bit  more uh relaxed than it had been of  course when it was it was never besieged  but the troops were in some parts uh  they were very close to the to the city  borders and um now this has changed so  the situation is is  is uh it's not normal of course many  people have left the city it's pretty  empty a lot of shops are closed and a  lot there's a curfew and so on and so on  but it doesn't feel as  critical as before having said that kiev  like any other city in ukraine is still  a target for missile attacks and just a  few days ago there was a missile attack  while the u.n secretary general was  there so there is of course uh it is of  course a wartime capital  and just to to move on to mario paul  where of course those holdout fighters  are being besieged i